Green: 625 passing, 0 failing, exit 0.

**What was broken:** one line in `src/pricing.js:39` — `orderTotal` taxed the pre-discount base and added the tax as a flat term, instead of taxing the discounted amount.

```js
// before
const discounted = applyDiscount(cents, discountPct);
const tax = roundCents(cents * taxRate);   // ← full base
return discounted + tax;

// after
const discounted = applyDiscount(cents, discountPct);
return applyTax(discounted, taxRate);
```

**Why the wall of text:** only 3 of 625 cases failed, all in `order totals`. Every other row in that suite has either a 0% discount or a 0 tax rate, and with either factor zero the buggy and correct formulas give the same answer. The three rows with both non-zero (`12000c/15%/8.25%`, `8650c/20%/5%`, `33400c/10%/20%`) were the only ones that could expose it — customers were being overcharged tax on the discount they'd been given (e.g. $367.40 instead of $360.72 on the last one).

Nothing else needed touching — the other eight suites and `src/tiers.js` were already correct. To skip the noise next time: `node run-tests.js | Select-String '^\s*FAIL'`.
